/target/
**/target/
# Local agent/runtime state is durable outside git only. Do not commit OMC/OMX
# plans, sessions, checkpoints, HUD state, logs, or verification scratch.
/.omc/*
!/.omc/ultragoal/
/.omc/ultragoal/*
!/.omc/ultragoal/OWNERS
!/.omc/ultragoal/TEAMMATE-PREAMBLE.md
!/.omc/ultragoal/friction-ledger.jsonl
!/.omc/ultragoal/premise.txt
/.omx/
# Local GJC runtime/session state is never committed.
# Specs/plans promoted to product authority belong in tracked specs/docs/registry files.
/.gjc/_session-*/
/.gjc/state/notifications/
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store

# Local secrets and credentials (never committed).
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.*.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.kubeconfig

.grit
/bominal/

# Python bytecode (per shell-python audit 2026-05-15)
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Transient session-scoped audit logs
.audit/
evidence/oci-readiness/a1-capacity-retry.log

# Atomic-write temp residue (write-then-rename crash debris).
# Pattern catches *.json.tmp.<uuid> and *.tmp.<uuid> shapes outside ignored
# runtime roots.
**/*.json.tmp.*

# Agent-spawned Claude Code worktrees (transient; each is a git worktree itself).
# .claude/settings.json (project-scoped) and .claude/commands/ remain tracked.
.claude/worktrees/

# Session-scoped Claude hook overrides are local-only; tracked project wiring stays authoritative.
.claude/settings.local.json

# Transient test output
test-results/

# ADR-0516 fabric drive-loop OPERATIONAL (execution) plane — repo-adjacent
# claim/heartbeat/run state per specs/fabric-drive-loop-state.json. Never
# committed: the durable coordination plane (plan/fabric-loop/) is the only
# PR-governed loop-state surface; this root is a local bridge store behind
# ExecutionPlanePort until the oya-cloud-ci-loop-state-service cutover.
/.oya-loop-state/

# Generated outputs default to untracked. Public/productized generated
# artifacts that must be committed are force-added intentionally and declared in
# registry/generated-artifact-control-plane.json, where cloud-ci enforces owner,
# generator, materialization, and merge policy. Keep this preventive layer aligned
# with the manifest's generated_path_rules; the Rust gate is authoritative.
**/generated/**
**/__generated__/**
**/generated-sources/**
**/generated-types/**
**/gen/**
**/*.generated.json
**/*.generated.ts
**/*.generated.d.ts
**/*.pb.go
**/*.pb.rs
!**/generated/
!**/generated/.gitkeep

# Rename-aware path-keyed CI baseline relabel move-manifest (task #64): a COMMITTED review
# artifact (the authoritative move bijection the scm-facts emitter relabel consumes), unlike
# the untracked per-checkout snapshots below. It is regenerated each PR run by the codemod
# `manifest` subcommand and byte-bound by the registry-drift/freshness committed==regenerated
# coverage + declared in registry/generated-artifact-control-plane.json, so it must be TRACKED
# (the control-plane gate's declared-path-must-be-tracked predicate). Negate the broad
# *.generated.json ignore for exactly this path.
!specs/reorg/move-manifest.generated.json

# FROZEN-REFERENCE RATCHET BASELINE — MUST stay TRACKED (dev hotfix to #828/ADR-0595). The
# gate-baseline face is NOT a pure view like the five faces below: it is the firewall ratchet's
# frozen reference, materialized by the scm-facts emitter via `git show <merge-base>:<this-path>`
# (oya-cloud-ci-scm-facts-emitter-app git_show_file). That merge-base materialization REQUIRES the
# path to be a committed git blob on the main branch. #828 de-committed it, so at gate-time
# `git cat-file -e <merge-base>:<path>` failed -> missing_at_merge_base=true -> empty frozen
# baseline -> every pre-existing repo-wide debt item reported as a NEW regression on every
# broad-affected-set PR. It is declared materialization_mode: main-branch-materialized in
# registry/generated-artifact-control-plane.json: committed on the integration branch for merge-base
# consumers, but controller-owned so contributor PRs do not carry generated baseline byte churn.
# Negate the broad *.generated.json ignore for exactly this path.
!ci/facade/artifact-inventory-registry/gate-baseline.generated.json

# ADR-0595/ADR-0597 de-commit class: the SIX cloud-ci faces below are pure derivations
# (git ls-files x OWNERS x ADR front-matter x specs). They were the #1 merge-conflict /
# merge-queue friction because every PR re-materialized multi-MB blobs. They are now DERIVED ON
# DEMAND (buck2 run //ci/facade/generated-artifact-freshness:oya-cloud-ci-materialize-generated-faces-bin) and materialized out-of-graph for
# consumers, whose gates re-derive content from the candidate tree; the freshness gate validates
# regenerate-success + regenerate-twice determinism instead of byte parity, and the control-plane
# gate forbids re-tracking them (materialization_mode: not-tracked-in-git). They are already
# covered by the **/*.generated.json rule above and are intentionally NOT negated here (unlike
# move-manifest and gate-baseline):
#   ci/facade/artifact-inventory-registry/accounting-registry.generated.json
#   ci/facade/artifact-inventory-registry/decision-crosswalk.generated.json
#   ci/facade/artifact-inventory-registry/enforcement-inventory.generated.json
#   ci/facade/artifact-inventory-registry/enforcement-liveness.generated.json
#   ci/facade/artifact-inventory-registry/ttl-policy.generated.json
#   ci/facade/artifact-inventory-registry/scm-facts.generated.json
# ADR-0597 (completes the ADR-0595 strangler): scm-facts.generated.json was the LAST committed
# pure-derivation face. It was kept committed in #828 only because it is a declared hermetic input
# to ~20 gate tests; those consumers now materialize it on demand (CI producer-regen uploads the
# materialized face; every gate matrix leg downloads it before `cargo test`). De-committing it
# removes the last shared committed merge surface, so a PR can no longer dirty every other open PR
# by re-materializing it — the faces-serialization cascade is now impossible. Unlike gate-baseline
# it is NOT a frozen ratchet reference (it is the SCM-facts snapshot the producer derives FROM,
# regenerated from `git ls-files` each run), so de-committing it does NOT trip the #831/ADR-0596
# frozen-reference guard.
# NOTE: gate-baseline.generated.json is NOT in this de-commit class — it is the frozen ratchet
# baseline and stays tracked (negated above).

# buck2 build output
/buck-out/

# Repo-root build/test SCRATCH artifacts (prevention layer; the cloud-ci-root-workspace-hygiene
# allowlist gate (ADR-0600) + the cloud-ci-total-accounting `scratch_artifact` frozen_empty code
# are the blocking backstops per enforcement-layering: automation default + blocking backstop).
# These root-anchored patterns block the slice-NN burndown / retest / lane-scratch class (#671
# G011 residue + the Jun-10 slice-6 logs + the *-targets.txt / premise / review-verdict pollution)
# from being staged again. Root-anchored so legitimately nested tracked files are untouched;
# force-add (`git add -f`) still routes the file through the allowlist gate, which is the
# construction layer that makes committed root scratch unmergeable (.gitignore alone cannot catch
# `git add -f` or already-tracked files — the gate is the real enforcement).
/*.log
/*.tmp
/*.out
/run-*.sh
/run-slice.sh
/retest-targets.txt
/*-targets.txt
/branch-wired-members.txt
/premise.txt
/review-verdict.txt
/slice*-*.log
/slice*-*.txt

# cloud-kernel QEMU/serial CONFORMANCE run output (build output, not evidence). The
# crate-local cloud/cloud-kernel/.gitignore ignores top-level /out/*.log but NOT the
# out/conformance/ subdir or the .txt report variants, which is how 50 conformance logs +
# stress-summary.txt slipped in via the bulk kernel import (#640). The tracked /out/*.elf
# carriers (include_bytes! build inputs) + musl-src/hello.c stay un-ignored in the crate
# .gitignore; this only adds the run-output subtree.
cloud/cloud-kernel/out/conformance/
cloud/cloud-kernel/out/stress-summary.txt

# Merge-base frozen-baseline snapshot (ADR-0551, FRIC-1781112000): a per-checkout derived
# reference materialized by the scm-facts emitter from `git merge-base <base_ref> HEAD`.
# It varies with the base branch position, so it can never be a committed face; CI
# rematerializes it before gates consume it.
ci/facade/baseline-ratchet/gate-baseline.merge-base.generated.json

# History-volatile SCM facts snapshot (ADR-0552, FRIC-1781234047): per-path last-touch
# revision ids + timestamps, rewritten by every squash-merge — a per-checkout derived input
# materialized by the scm-facts emitter, so it can never be a committed face; CI
# rematerializes it before gates consume it.
ci/facade/scm-facts-snapshot/scm-volatile-facts.generated.json

# Dev-only Asterinas boot-harness receipts are regenerable run outputs (reference target/ logs); not committed.
kernel/harness/*/receipts/
